"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[9632],{9632:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"zanyatost-ssha-sentyabr-realnye-zarplaty","locale":"en","title":"US job creation is 3 times below expectations while wages lose ground to prices","description":"The US added 29 thousand September jobs against a 90 thousand forecast; wages rose 3% with inflation at 3.4%. What real wages mean and what may happen to Fed rates.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"On October 2, 2026, the US Labor Department reported that the economy created 29 thousand jobs in September, versus expectations of about 90 thousand. July and August figures were revised down by a combined 60 thousand. Unemployment rose from 4.1% to 4.2%. Healthcare added the most jobs, 17 thousand, followed by construction with 11 thousand, while finance shed 7 thousand."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"Wages are the weakest part of September\'s report. Average hourly earnings rose by only 0.1% over the month, the slowest increase since December 2025. Annual wage growth was 3%, its weakest since May 2021. Meanwhile, US prices are rising by 3.4% annually according to the latest August data. An American\'s wages buy less than a year earlier."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"That is the distinction between nominal and real wages. Nominal wages are the amount on a payslip. Real wages show what that amount buys, subtracting price growth from wage growth. Comparing September wage growth with August inflation suggests real US wages are falling by about 0.4% a year (1.03 / 1.034). In Russia, average July 2026 wages increased by 9.5% to 109.5 thousand rubles, while real wages rose by 3.3%. The comparison is approximate because months and calculation methods differ. Russian growth also slowed slightly, from 3.4% in June."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"For the US Federal Reserve, a weak labor market argues against haste. Over a week, markets\' estimate of a rate increase at the October 27–28 meeting fell from 64% to about 20%, first after inflation data and then the employment report. But inflation of 3.4% remains well above the 2% target, so markets expect a postponement rather than abandonment: major banks such as Goldman Sachs still anticipate a December increase. The 10-year Treasury yield initially fell after the report but finished the day at 5.28%. The Fed\'s current rate is 3.75–4%."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"For Russian readers, the US report matters through the dollar, pulling it in different directions. Postponing a rate increase makes the dollar slightly less attractive; on Monday, October 5, it weakened a little against other currencies. But US bonds still pay more than 5%, supporting demand for dollars. Oil and Bank of Russia decisions have greater influence on the ruble, Russian prices and rates. The next US employment report arrives on November 6, after the October Fed meeting."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"Dollar holders face a choice. Selling after a weak report means betting that the Fed will abandon rate increases entirely, which nobody has promised. Buying in anticipation of a stronger dollar is also risky: if unemployment keeps rising, the Fed could cancel a December increase too. Whether labor-market weakness becomes a trend is still unknown."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"How many jobs did the US create in September 2026?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"29 thousand against a forecast of about 90 thousand. July and August figures were revised down by 60 thousand, and unemployment rose from 4.1% to 4.2%."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"What are real wages?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"Wages adjusted for price growth, meaning the amount they can buy. US wages rose by 3% over the year while inflation was 3.4%, so real wages fell by about 0.4%. Russian real wages rose by 3.3% in July."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"Will the Fed raise rates after the weak jobs report?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"Probably not in October: markets estimate the probability at about 20%, versus 64% a week earlier. But markets and major banks still expect a December increase. The current Fed rate is 3.75–4%."}],"sources":[{"label":"September\'s jobs report misses: US added just 29,000 jobs, unemployment ticked up","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/article/septembers-jobs-report-shows-the-us-added-just-29000-jobs-and-unemployment-ticked-up-195320409.html"},{"label":"Inflation has been eating up wage gains for months. September was no better","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/article/inflation-has-been-eating-up-wage-gains-for-months-september-was-no-better-180727718.html"},{"label":"World Economy Latest: US employers dial back hiring, wage growth slows","url":"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-03/world-economy-latest-us-employers-dial-back-hiring-wage-growth-slows"},{"label":"Nasdaq Adds 319 Points as Rate-Hike Odds Ebb","url":"https://www.kiplinger.com/investing/stocks/nasdaq-adds-319-points-as-rate-hike-odds-ebb-stock-market-today"},{"label":"The October Fed hike just died. Here\'s what the 29K jobs report really means for rates","url":"https://www.fxstreet.com/analysis/the-october-fed-hike-just-died-heres-what-the-29k-jobs-report-really-means-for-rates-202610021806"},{"label":"Treasury Yields Drop as Weak Jobs Report Eases October Fed Rate Hike Odds","url":"https://www.indexbox.io/blog/treasury-yields-fall-after-weak-september-jobs-report-cuts-odds-of-october-fed-rate-hike/"},{"label":"Stocks upbeat, dollar wobbles as Fed hike bets recede","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy-news/stocks-upbeat-dollar-wobbles-as-fed-hike-bets-recede-4930982"},{"label":"Schedule of Releases for the Employment Situation","url":"https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/empsit.htm"},{"label":"Russian real-wage growth slows to 3.3% year-on-year in July","url":"https://ru.themoscowtimes.com/2026/09/30/rost-realnykh-zarplat-v-rf-v-iyule-26g-zamedlilsya-do-33-gg-a207452"}],"sourceBodySha256":"8dbaae3cc9570f53146a348a9d62855bcdad77232b7be2422c1b98c268553b25"}')}}]);